[#:seon.task{:name "a-failure-attaches-a-refinement",
             :plan
             "Lane AGENTS (in flight). inv1: on any failed attempt the reconciler writes :seon.task/execution :held over the owner's release (:bail, reconcile.clj:366-384, :523-524; merge-train refusal :617-619), nothing re-releases it, and its dependents wait forever with no record. DECISIONS: nothing is held for release or relaunched; a failure attaches new tasks worked by new agents from the improved plan and the evidence. Attach a refinement chain until the task's declared budget (:seon.task/budget, replacing :max-attach) is spent.",
             :kind :work,
             :proofs
             #{seon.reconcile-test/a-capped-attempt-attaches-a-refinement-not-a-hold}}
