             "Seen (e5_tasks E5.B, e7 E7.2): with an attempt's failure recorded with the program t it ran on, the readiness rule 'never ran, or failed on a program older than main's' re-runs exactly the failed task and what it blocked when a fix merges (E7.2 re-ran :orphan and :pid-check only). Today a stuck task needs a person (seon.reconcile idx-ready? requires (nil? :seon.task/stuck)). Correct: :seon.attempt records main's program t; a stuck task whose program t is older than main's is ready again (its budget counts attempts per program).",
