 {:seon.task/name "contract-gaps-have-one-rule"
  :seon.task/plan "Seen 2026-10-21 by lane AGENTS: which contract gaps an attempt answers for is decided in three places. The turn loop takes harvest/uncontracted now minus the gaps when the attempt began (seon.turn/begin!, observe, turn.clj); root's judge takes the branch's program entries that have no contract and differ from main's (judge-tx, reconcile.clj:588-600); and before e37b318 the door's context read took every gap (it showed 400 seeded app.m*/f* gaps from seon.db's seed program as refusals). Two rules can disagree: a gap main gained after the branch point, or a var the agent re-evaluated unchanged. Correct: one function, the judge's (gaps on the branch's program entries that differ from main's base), called by the turn loop, the context and the judge alike. Deletes :gaps-before."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.reconcile-test/the-loop-the-context-and-the-judge-name-the-same-gaps}}
 {:seon.task/name "render-reads-the-reconcilers-index"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-10-21 by lane RENDER on its own root (bin/root, 92 tasks, 13 attempts, 17 agents, 1,820 datoms; 20-run means through the door): seon.render.proc/main-info costs 113 ms per main commit, rebuilding from main's db what the reconciler already keeps incrementally: seon.reconcile/index 58 ms, seon.task/tasks 26 ms, seon.task/attempts 8 ms, seon.problems/report 5 ms, the datom count 0.7 ms (render/proc.clj main-info). A quiet render pass is 0.87 ms, so the commit path dominates. Build once: the reconciler emits each task row (state, blocked-by, proofs green/red/allowed, attempts, tokens), each attempt and the recorded problems as it changes them, through THREADS' event pillar, and render reads them; render's task-rows, its index rebuild and its per-commit seon.task/tasks and attempts go. Estimate: per main commit, work in proportion to the tasks and attempts that commit touched, not the whole index."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/render-rebuilds-no-index-per-commit
                      seon.render-test/render-main-commit-cost}}]
